confirms green status.\n./skills/review-library-bulk-update/SKILL.md:106:Ask for rerun or deeper investigation when:\n./skills/review-library-bulk-update/SKILL.md:117:- Flaky CI: leave a short comment requesting or noting a rerun.\n./skills/close-human-intervention-and-failing-ci-prs/SKILL.md:37:   - If the repository has more open PRs than the limit, rerun with a higher\n./skills/review-code-coverage-improvement/SKILL.md:38:  `N/A`. `N/A` means the native build in the stats step failed; ask for a rerun\n./skills/review-code-coverage-improvement/SKILL.md:153:- `dynamicAccess.coverageRatio` regressed or became `N/A` (ask for a rerun).\n./forge/README.md:172:unpublished results without rerunning coverage:\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/benchmarking.md:288:publication without rerunning coverage; a workspace without one is listed as\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/publication.md:67:(§FS-forge-run-requirements.4), reruns that gate exactly once, and lets only the\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/publication.md:68:rerun's outcome reach metadata repair or human intervention\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/publication.md:303:coordinate, so a rerun is possible after the gate exits whatever its status.\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/publication.md:397:finalization receipt, and owns staging and commits. A changed tree reruns only\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/publication.md:598:**Failed CI enters diagnosis immediately.** Forge does not rerun a failed\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/publication.md:610:validates those IDs and requests reruns of their failed jobs, then stops until a\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/publication.md:611:later pass. The analysis agent decides whether a rerun is justified, while Forge\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:298:reruns. That CI-repair turn receives the failed-check evidence, applies the same\n./forge/docs/functional-spec/continuation.md:37:| `setup` | discrete | Skip the sub-steps already marked done (`preflightDone`, `setupDone`); otherwise